# General Rules

- Look for and always follow all appliccable documentation inside /docs root folder of any project, or at root. - Only read docs based on their name you feel are relevant to your current context, do not waste tokens.
- There is a [docs/](../../docs) folder in this ai-shared project which is attached to vs code workspaces so you may access it. Docs here apply to general platform wide architectures
- Apply strong documentation and self documenting code techniques throughout this repository. Do not "over document" like a juinor engineer, clean and informative comments only where required for complex logic, and always dart docs for exposed APIs

---

# Project Overview

- This is a SaaS platform for Point of Sale both internal and customer facing tools
- There is a POS, a Kiosk, a Web App, and a Mobile App all built with Flutter
- There is a Portal / Backoffice and a C# backend

---

# Architecture Overview

- Flutter implements some custom Clean Architecture approach using riverpod for state management
- Build runner is heavily used for code generation

